    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0203" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg87"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 793.94/226.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Guthrie to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-11T16:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1915—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram of February 1, 11 a.m. The authority mentioned therein has just
                    informed me that he has authority for the conviction that the statement given me
                    by the Foreign Minister and cabled under date of February 9, midnight, does not
                    contain all of Japan’s demands but that there are others whose exact nature he
                    cannot state. Baron Kato has instructed the Japanese Minister at Peking to
                    communicate the statement given me to Reinsch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
